slackresolve (ELF dependency resolver for Slackware)

SlackResolve finds official Slackware packages that provide missing
files or ELF libraries. It can inspect one installed program, search
for a file, audit package-owned ELF objects, or analyze a package
before installation.

The resolver obtains repository information and packages through
slackpkg. It uses readelf and the native Slackware package records
instead of package dependency metadata. Plans can be reviewed before
installpkg or upgradepkg is called.

Version 0.4.0 builds a persistent provider index from the official
Slackware MANIFEST files, resolves unique dependencies in batches,
reuses downloaded packages and ELF analysis, and can continue an
interrupted resolution from an automatic checkpoint. Use
"slackresolve sessions" to list saved sessions and
"slackresolve resume SESSION_ID" to continue one.

SlackResolve is written in Bash and awk. It requires only software
included with a full Slackware 15.0 installation. A configured
slackpkg mirror and updated repository indexes are required for
searches and downloads.

Run the terminal interface with:

  slackresolve-tui

The command line interface is installed as /usr/sbin/slackresolve.

SlackResolve detects the target package architecture. It supports
x86_64, the 32-bit x86 family from i386 through i686, noarch packages,
and other Slackware architectures whose package architecture matches
the target. The package itself is noarch because it contains shell and
awk programs.

